Foundation decisions
Id	Question	Resolution	Source
scope	what is converted	the whole of the TracesData and LogsData lines that carry the 8, so the MTSV stands alone and the JSON can be dropped	owner, 2026-09-23
F1	the key of every row	address: a JSON Pointer from the file, first token the line, to the OTLP structure the row is or belongs to; pointer: within an attribute's or body's value, once one JSON value; key: on the rows of ordinary attributes, which are unordered and identified by key. The 8's rows keep address and pointer, their sheet naming the key	RFC 6901; CODD1970 1.3 primary key; OTEL-COMMON › Attribute Collections
F1 name	the column record	renamed address, since the draft calls a row a record; no source names this column	MTSV-DRAFT › Conventions and Definitions
F2	one-to-one objects: resource, scope, status	child sheets, a nested object being a relation of one row, as the server tool call details are	CODD1970 1.3 block 33
F3	lists of simple values: idKeys, descriptionKeys	child sheets, one value per row	CODD1970 1.4
F4	attributes other than the 8	the owner's attributes sheet: address, key, pointer, type, value; the 8 are recognized on spans and log records only, where OTEL-GENAI defines them, and appear only in their own sheets	OTEL-COMMON; OTEL-GENAI
F5	enums	written as the integers OTLP requires	OTLP docs/specification › JSON Protobuf Encoding
F6	metrics	a MetricsData line yields no rows	OTEL-FILE-EXPORTER › Telemetry data requirements; OTEL-GENAI
lines	which fields have lines sheets	the fields the source types as string, and every node value; ids (bytes), times, counts, flags and enums have none, as score has none	the protos; line.1
names	sheet names	full parent paths of the OTLP JSON keys (CODD1970 R.d); the 8 keep their attribute key alone, both spans and log records holding them	CODD1970 1.4 blocks 15-17
order	sheet order	the traces tree, then the logs tree, then the 8's sheets; each sheet followed by its lines sheets	file.4; line.1
span events	the 8 on a Span.Event	ordinary attributes: OTEL-GENAI defines the 8 on spans and on log-record events only	OTEL-GENAI
limits	what is not carried	int and double both a number, bytes a Base64 string (OTEL-COMMON: lossy); unknown fields; a JSON-string attribute's original whitespace; HT, FF and a CR alone; null, "" and absent alike	OTEL-COMMON; OTLP; MTSV-DRAFT
register	the fill the apply needs	resource.proto added to OTLP; fact rows for the OTLP messages and the UTF-8 rule; the protos stay single code blocks	open-telemetry/opentelemetry-proto at commit 700dafd2e89ad6266049000c616a589d884523d4, opentelemetry/proto/resource/v1/resource.proto
